      "created_at": "2016-01-18T06:43:49.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>No, because they are untyped cards while facedown. That's all that matters. They would be villain CARDS, though, which is what actually matters. So still yes, actually.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>As Ronway pointed out when discussing incapacitated Santa Guise's ability to flip face down cards, most cards like Savage Mana and La Capitan never specify that the cards are put there facedown.</p>",
